{
  "description": "Records anchored end to end on anvil (Anchor §6 to §10, §13): each record's envelope with its nonRepudiation.anchor, the epochs its anchors name (the anchor checkpoint, P, the consistency proofs between published sizes and between a source log's anchored checkpoints), and each epoch's evm-calldata/1 publication with its heavy material. A verifier must: parse every checkpoint body; place each record's canonicalDigest at leafIndex = sequenceNumber - 1 in its logCheckpoint (logPath) and SHA-256(logCheckpoint) at anchorLeafIndex in its anchorCheckpoint (anchorPath); check P = SHA-256(anchorCheckpoint); verify each consistency proof with both sizes and roots taken from the bodies; check keccak256(blockHeader) = blockHash and the header's number; walk txProof from the header's transactionsRoot at key rlp(txIndex) to rawTransaction; recover the sender from rawTransaction and find it in the manifest for the anchor origin, on the chain it signed; check its calldata is exactly 0x || P; and give every record the verdicts in expect: bundleOnly with the manifest and the publication's material, withHeaderSource with those and a header source that reports canonicalBlock and a finalized height of headerSource.finalizedBlockNumber.",
  "source": "Generated by scripts/generate-anchor-e2e-vectors.ts from one run of @tzun/sdk's anchor scheduler, through Tzun.init({ logNamespace: 'test.vectors.tzun', anchoring }), on anvil (ghcr.io/foundry-rs/foundry:v1.5.1, chain id 31337, --slots-in-an-epoch 1, so its finalized tag is the head minus 2). The publisher is anvil's development account 5. The values are that run's; the expected verdicts are stated from Anchor §10, and the script stopped unless the SDK's verifyAnchor agreed with every one. scripts/regenerate-vectors.ts does not rewrite this file.",
  "format": {
    "records": "envelope is the stored record; its nonRepudiation.anchor is tzun-anchor/1 §8.1. epoch indexes epochs.",
    "epochs": "anchorCheckpoint is the anchor log at its published size; p = SHA-256(anchorCheckpoint), 64 lowercase hex, and the publication's calldata. previousAnchorSize is the previous published size (null for the first) and anchorConsistencyProof is PROOF(previousAnchorSize, size) (empty for the first). members are the source-log checkpoints this epoch appended, in anchor-leaf order: previousLogCheckpoint is that log's previous anchored checkpoint (null for its first) and consistencyProof is PROOF between the two (empty for the first). Hashes are bare lowercase hex, except the EVM values, which are 0x-prefixed.",
    "publication": "The evm-calldata/1 entry as a record carries it (tzun-anchor/1 §8.2: kind, chain, transactionId, blockNumber, blockHash, publisher) joined with the export bundle's heavy material (rawTransaction, blockHeader: the header RLP, txIndex, txProof: the transactions-trie nodes from the root, each RLP).",
    "canonicalBlock": "What anvil reported for the publication's block number when the file was made: its hash and its timestamp (unix seconds).",
    "headerSource": "The header source a withHeaderSource verdict uses: chainId, the finalized height, and for each epoch's block the canonicalBlock; it looks no transaction up."
  },
